Breakthrough Action Nigeria (BA-N) is a USAID funded Social Behaviour Change (SBC) and Risk Communication Project with the goal of increasing practice of priority individual and household level health behaviours in target states on MNCH+N, FP, Malaria, Tuberculosis, priority zoonotic diseases; and the COVID-19 response. Firmly grounded in proven practices, Breakthrough ACTION works in partnership with governments, civil society, and communities around the world to implement creative and sustainable SBC programming, nurture SBC champions, mainstream new techniques, and technologies, and advocate strategic and sustained investment in SBC.
Breakthrough ACTION Nigeria supports the development and strengthening of National and State health security capacities to prevent, detect, and respond to threats against their health and safety, working closely with the International Health Regulations (IHR) National Focal Point and National One Health Coordination Unit (NOHCU) for implementation of RCCE-related activities in national policies e.g. One Health Strategic Plan; National Action Plan for Health Security and Joint External Evaluation Report.
Scope of Work
The RCCE Consultant will work at the country office to provide required technical and strategic level coordination for GHSA work stream implementation including technical assistance to diverse stakeholders, support for documentation and learning, and Research/Human Centred Design (HCD) activity as it relates to all BA-N Risk Communication and Community Engagement activities.
