LOCATION:
Victoria Island, Lagos
DEPARTMENT:
Marketing and Brands
ABOUT US
Redwire is a strategic marketing and brand design consultancy in Nigeria. We help clients learn more about their brands, customers, businesses, and communications and then maximize these assets to improve performance and increase profits. We know the science of marketing, but we know the art of it too and are highly skilled at fusing the two for our clients’ benefit. Please see www.redwire-group.com
POSITION OVERVIEW
The Marketing Associate is responsible for managing the art and science of marketing to solve clients marketing needs. S/he will work with managers to oversee the implementation of marketing plans, including promotional materials, advertising opportunities, and client acquisition.
ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS
Create marketing proposals;
Oversee and develop marketing campaigns and proposals;
Write and proofread thought leadership marketing articles;
Attend client meetings to understand clients’ needs for briefs;
Create communications and operations plans for clients;
Conceive, develop and implement efficient and intuitive marketing strategies;
Manage tasks administration to ensure the Marketing department runs smoothly;
Conduct brainstorming sessions with the team, maintaining strategic and creative thinking to develop innovative and actionable plans in a fiscally responsible manner;
Conduct research and analyze data to identify and define audiences;
Monitor progress of campaigns using various metrics and submits reports of performance;
Oversee the production of all marketing materials, including printed documents, media advertising spots, website content, and social media accounts;
Perform promotional activities for clients;
Organize events and product exhibitions;
Supervise a cross-functional team of designers, marketers and digital marketers;
Travel to meet clients and attend conferences, workshops, trade shows, industry events, and seminars;
Monitor competitor activity and brainstorm potential improvements or changes in marketing strategy, products, or services.
EDUCATION:
Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Marketing, PR or related fields.
WORK EXPERIENCE:
Minimum of 3
years’
Marketing experience in a consulting capacity
KNOWLEDGE REQUIREMENTS:
Strong understanding of modern marketing processes and technology capabilities around the following areas: Marketing Resource Management, Marketing Analytics, and Customer Data Management
Proven experience/knowledge of CRM and Marketing Automation tools
Professional competency in the management and execution of complex projects, consulting internal clients, and management of multiple resources.
SKILL REQUIREMENTS:
Exceptional interpersonal skills with the proven ability to work in a team environment;
High attention to detail
Leadership
Creative and Strategic Thinking
Passionate, Dynamic & Proactive
Receptive to Change
Excellent Communication and Public Speaking

PRO-Cashew Project
CNFA is implementing the PRO-Cashew project funded by the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) for a period of five years. The PRO-Cashew project will contribute to strengthening the competitiveness of West African producers by improving the efficiency and quality of production and trade, and by developing more coherent regional trade and investment policies. In doing so, the project will build producer capacity and develop incentives to renovate and rehabilitate cashew farms, improve production and quality, and create a more competitive West African raw cashew nut for the international market.
General Responsibilities:
